{"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"missing-failure-contract","classStatement":"The acceptance criteria omit an explicitly required failure condition that must prevent a successful verdict.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC2 (lines 41–46) and R4 (line 83) cover missing tooling and incomplete-run/parse-error smells but omit sensor crashes. requirements/design.md:49 explicitly requires any sensor crash to produce UNAVAILABLE.","failureScenario":"A sensor crashes without emitting an incomplete-run or parse-error smell -> an implementation can satisfy the listed tests while treating absent findings as an empty successful result and reporting PASS.","id":"F1","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"incomplete-initialization-contract","classStatement":"Initialization omits a prerequisite required by the analysis configuration it generates.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC6 (lines 60–66) requires type-aware ESLint rules but neither creates a TypeScript program configuration nor specifies a follow-up action for it; only dogfood AC8 requires a tsconfig. requirements/design.md:103 requires allowJs/checkJs and projectService for JavaScript repositories. Plan P3 likewise omits this setup.","failureScenario":"A fresh JavaScript repository runs init and installs every dependency named by its follow-up message -> type-aware linting still lacks the required TypeScript program and the wrapper remains UNAVAILABLE instead of completing the documented setup path.","id":"F2","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"approval-selection-contradiction","classStatement":"Accumulated approval forwarding contradicts the wrapper's mismatch rule and prevents later valid approvals from taking effect.","document":"requirements/plan.md","evidence":"P4 (line 48) passes --approved for every recorded config approval. Spec AC2 (line 46) requires UNAVAILABLE when a supplied approval mismatches the current subject, while AC4 (line 54) promises that approving the current change makes the next run count it.","failureScenario":"A human approves configuration A, later edits it to B and approves B -> the core supplies both approvals; stale approval A mismatches B, so the wrapper remains UNAVAILABLE despite the valid current approval.","id":"F3","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"waiver-coverage-contradiction","classStatement":"The criteria accept a waived failure while requiring an incompatible passing receipt for final coverage.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC8 and R11 (lines 74 and 90) accept dogfooding with a FAIL plus recorded waiver. AC5 (line 59) requires a passing same-tree final code-health receipt for CI coverage. AC3's waiver (line 50) only specifies round qualification and preserves the original outcome; no criterion explains coverage of the retained FAIL.","failureScenario":"Trent waives a deterministic code-health regression on the final candidate -> AC8/R11 declare the dogfood evidence acceptable, but the final receipt remains FAIL and cannot meet AC5's passing-receipt condition.","id":"F4","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"nonbinary-rubric","classStatement":"Rubric fail conditions do not cover realistic outcomes excluded by their pass conditions.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"R11 (line 90) passes only PASS or FAIL with a recorded waiver, but fails only UNAVAILABLE or missing receipt, leaving an unwaived FAIL unclassified. R9 (line 88) requires a valid vendored plugin and follow-up message to pass, but its fail conditions cover only missing/overwritten files and wrong limits.","failureScenario":"Dogfooding returns an unwaived FAIL, or init writes all files with correct limits but an invalid plugin -> the corresponding rubric row satisfies neither its stated pass nor fail conditions, preventing a binary acceptance decision.","id":"F5","severity":"medium"}],"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The proposed approach stays within the feature goal and recorded design amendment C1: wrapper-based Verification, governed-config approval, human opt-out, plugin, doctor and dogfooding. requirements/plan.md:26 reserves the final integration-to-main merge for Trent's per-PR instruction; its slice branches avoid development/development-* branches. Installation is limited to local dogfood/testing setup, with no automatic user-environment installation or other prohibited action proposed.","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"All rubric rows have plan and issue mappings, but implementation authorization is blocked by missing crash handling and TypeScript setup requirements, contradictory approval and waiver behavior, and nonbinary rubric conditions."}